<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro IV of Kongo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1718">1718</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro IV was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> from 1695 to 1718, ruling from the mountain stronghold of Kibangu during the civil wars that followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mbwila">Battle of Mbwila</a>. He worked to reconcile the rival royal houses and in 1709 reoccupied São <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, having earlier had the prophet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kimpa-vita">Kimpa Vita</a>, leader of the Antonian movement, burnt as a heretic in 1706.</p></div>
